 built in. Each short unit costs 22 against the baseline: 15 of lost revenue plus 7 of penalty.\n  - Candidates 0 and 1 order about 1.0×.\n  - Candidate 5 orders about 1.07×. It ends with about 60 extra units, which cost 11 each, and it carries a larger buffer at 0.8 per day.\n- To compare plans, I used the identity profit ≈ const + price × orders − (price + penalty) × end stock − holding. By that estimate, candidate 0 beats candidate 2 by about 200 on product 0 and about 100 on product 1. It beats candidate 3 by more on both.\n- Candidate 0 also orders less at the end (25 and 45), which cuts waste of stock that would go unsold after day 29.\n\n**Candidate 1** is almost the same as candidate 0, just shifted by a day. Its totals match candidate 0's (888/874 against 891/870). But it has 15 order days instead of 14, and the extra one, on day 27, is only for 12 units of product 1. So it comes out about 56 worse than candidate 0.\n\n**Candidate 0** has the highest expected profit. Candidate 2 is the main competitor because demand is random."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3830, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2304, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 3830}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-19T07:42:17.022Z", "request_id": "req_011CgBDXVd46CVm2eU2hXFU6"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_012Wqm2NVCnecPVgWhnBdUQ4", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assist