.10× (949) | ≈1.00× (832) |\n| 3 | ≈1.00× (846) | ≈1.00× (832) |\n| 5 | ≈1.10× (949) | ≈1.10× (925) |\n\nExpected demand is about 880 for product 0 (days 3–29) and about 865 for product 1 (days 2–29).\n\n**Product 1** (margin 4, shortage penalty 7, storage 0.8 a day). Spare stock is expensive to hold. Compared with candidate 0, ordering exactly the forecast (candidates 2 and 3) adds about 25 units of shortage, costing about −554. It buys 38 fewer units (+418) and holds about 17 fewer units a day (+380). Net, about **+245** for candidates 2 and 3. Ordering 1.10× (candidate 5) is clearly worse, which rules out 5.\n\n**Product 0** (margin 8, penalty 5, storage 0.3 a day). Compared with candidate 0:\n- **Candidate 2 (1.10×):** cuts shortage from about 28 to about 7 units (+385) but buys 58 more units (−290) and stores more (−200). Net about **−107**.\n- **Candidate 3 (1.00×):** shortage rises to about 57 units (−522), offset by buying less (+225) and storing less (+138). Net about **−159**.\n\nCandidate 2 overflows the 216-unit warehouse on day 21. The lost units would mostly have been left over anyway, so that costs only a few tens.\n\n**Totals against candidate 0:**\n- Candidate 2: about +138\n- Candidate 3: about +86\n- Candidate 0: 0\n- Candidate 1: about −56\n- Candidates 5, 4, 6 and 7: lower"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 356, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5699, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 356}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-19T07:48:40.822Z", "request_id": "req_011CgBDnTXxoNnPjjioKkKSJ"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "str